meta {
  name: GET trips shortterm last (#1805)
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/vehicle/v1/trips/{{vin}}/shortterm/last
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  #1805: the address the Audi app reads the last short-term trip from
  (myAudi 5.9.0). The trip type is in lower case. The answer carries the
  trip, or a list of trips, under "data".

  The integration asks this address only when
  /vehicle/v1/vehicles/{vin}/tripstatistics?type=shortTerm answers 404.
  A 404 here, or an answer without a trip, ends it: the long-term and
  cyclic addresses are then not asked.

  Read from the app's request format. Not confirmed on a car.

  Implementation: VWEUClient._fetch_trips_app_route() in
  cariad/api/vw_eu.py. Audi inherits.
}
